  "solution_principle": "Assignment 3:\r\n\r\n1- Build a grid of hexagonal cells: Size 10, 15 Ex, 15 Ex\r\n\r\n2- Right-Click on the C OUTPUT and select \"Flatten\".\r\n\r\n3- Use a (2-True/2-False) pattern to cull cells.\r\n\r\n4- Extract the center points' coordinates of the resultant cells.\r\n\r\n5- Select only the ones with the same X value of your choice (take a look at the X vlues and pick one value).\r\n\r\n6- Jitter the resultant Points.\r\n\r\n7- Organize them from smallest to largest Y value.\r\n\r\n8- Find the length of the List of Points and split the List in half.\r\n\r\nExtra step:\r\n9- Select the cells belonging to the first half as of step (8) and extrude them by their area value in the Z direction.",
